{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Onka's Big Moka is an album released in 1999 by the post-Britpop band Toploader.","title":"Onka's Big Moka"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The album reached #4 on the UK charts, and a song from the album, "Dancing in the Moonlight", a cover of the King Harvest song, was featured in a television commercial for supermarket chain Sainsbury's and on the soundtrack of the 2002 American coming-of-age teen romantic drama "A Walk to Remember".","title":"Onka's Big Moka"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Gandugali Kumara Rama is a 2006 Indian biographical historical drama film based on the life of Kumara Rama (1290 AD – 1320 AD), who is considered to be the warrior prince prior to the establishment of the Vijayanagara Empire.","title":"Gandugali Kumara Rama"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Directed by H. R. Bhargava and produced by Anitha Pattabhiram, the film threads the path of a novel written by Su.","title":"Gandugali Kumara Rama"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Rudramurthy Shastry.","title":"Gandugali Kumara Rama"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The film featured Shivarajkumar as the lead in dual roles along with Rambha, Laya and Anitha in pivotal roles.","title":"Gandugali Kumara Rama"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" The film was declared an average grosser by box office report.","title":"Gandugali Kumara Rama"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" It was during the filming of this movie that Shivrajkumar's father and veteran actor Dr Rajkumar died.","title":"Gandugali Kumara Rama"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"White Noise is a song by American rock band Linkin Park, which was released on October 17, 2014 through Warner Bros.","title":"White Noise (Linkin Park song)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Records and Machine Shop Records.","title":"White Noise (Linkin Park song)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The song was released in the promotion of a 2014 American drama film based on a novel written by Eric Bogosian named as "Mall".","title":"White Noise (Linkin Park song)"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The song is one of the four unreleased demos by the band included in the original motion picture soundtrack to the same name of the film.","title":"White Noise (Linkin Park song)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Quiet & Still is Magnet's debut album, first released in Norway in October 2000 after the dissolution of his previous band Libido.","title":"Quiet &amp; Still"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" In the US, the album was released under his birth name, Even Johansen, and featured his picture on the album cover (whereas the Norwegian release featured a logo).","title":"Quiet &amp; Still"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The album features early versions of "Where Happiness Lives" and "Nothing Hurts Now," which he would re-record for the follow-up album "On Your Side".","title":"Quiet &amp; Still"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" It also features a cover of "Dancing in the Moonlight," written by Thin Lizzy frontman Phil Lynott.","title":"Quiet &amp; Still"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"A Walk to Remember is a 2002 American coming-of-age romantic drama film directed by Adam Shankman and written by Karen Janszen, based on Nicholas Sparks' 1999 novel of the same name.","title":"A Walk to Remember"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The film stars Shane West, Mandy Moore, Peter Coyote and Daryl Hannah, and was produced by Denise Di Novi and Hunt Lowry for Warner Bros.","title":"A Walk to Remember"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Pictures.","title":"A Walk to Remember"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Vennello Aadapilla (English: "Lady in the moonlight") is written by Yandamoori Veerendranath.","title":"Vennello Adapilla"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" This is a romantic novel written in Telugu which contains drama, knowledge, information, suspense and more.","title":"Vennello Adapilla"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Based on this novel, a serial was also made, for which the author received the Nandi award for the Best Director.","title":"Vennello Adapilla"}],"peer_messages":["Unverified peer answer: Nicholas Spa